    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "940741c2_b593afd7",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1095,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-18T06:57:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do not understand the implications of having this call here.  If we have disabled a BSSID, this implies we want to scan.  But since this is an async flow, we could be handling a failure that might have come in since we had selected another ssid or bssid.  It seems like scheduling a scan here is risky.\n\nWith this code:\n        if (mWifiState \u003d\u003d WIFI_STATE_DISCONNECTED) {\n            mLastConnectionAttemptBssid \u003d null;\n            scheduleWatchdogTimer();\n            startConnectivityScan(SCAN_IMMEDIATELY);\n\naren\u0027t we issuing 2 scan requests?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1090,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1095,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "f5a396c13ff5000ec7fb4bcce26508df7872074b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
